      "feedback": "Here is the evaluation for the Fiji Fan Palm (Pritchardia pacifica) data payload, focusing on content integrity, structural gaps, and multi-channel readiness.\n\nStrengths\nCanoe Plant & Cultural Narrative: Excellent historical framing—explaining how ancient Polynesian voyagers transported the seeds across open oceans and detailing the royal ai viu ceremonial fan/umbrella usage makes the content engaging.\n\nIn-Field Key Diagnostic: The comparison with Thurston’s Fan Palm (Pritchardia thurstonii) is outstanding. Highlighting that flower clusters stay tucked inside the crown (vs. arching outward 2 meters on P. thurstonii) gives visitors and staff a definitive visual diagnostic.\n\nLethal Yellowing Context: Accurately highlights high susceptibility to phytoplasma spread by the planthopper (Haxius crudus / Myndus crudus), providing essential disease risk context for Florida growers.\n\nCritical Missing Content & Practical Gaps\nLethal Yellowing & Microclimate Realities in Zone 10A\n\nMissing: Cold to",
